# 2. What the tests are made of (no network, no real GitLab or AWS anywhere)
The test file builds three kinds of worlds: (a) the pure parts and the seed (the seed is built from the real files of this tree and its `npm test` is run with the real node in a temporary directory with no install, with an explicit environment so that a child `node --test` does not inherit NODE_TEST_CONTEXT); (b) real temporary git repositories holding the real seed, in which the commits the script would send to the Commits API are applied the way GitLab applies them, and the functions of the merge bot are imported and run on them (commitsInRange, judgeReviewCommit, localAfter, reviewCurrent, decide, checksFor, laneKeyOf, protectedTouched, PROTECTED_GATE_PATHS, GOVERNANCE_PATHS, isSessionId); (c) whole runs of run() against a fake GitLab built on scripts/eng/testing/fake-fetch.mjs (commits with trees, branches, merge requests, events, pipelines, jobs, comments), a scripted merge bot with the reasons in the order of mergeDecision, a fleet that boots machines (cap 24, auto-cancel of older pipelines, idle time, spot-like staggered boots), a fake aws runner and a virtual clock. globalThis.fetch is replaced by a function that throws for the duration of every whole run.
The sample outputs are produced by the same worlds: outputs/report-sample-simulated.txt, outputs/report-sample-asg-denied.txt, outputs/dry-run-sample.txt, outputs/refusal-sample.txt. They show the FORMAT of the report. They are a simulation and not the owner's run; the owner's run on the real system is what proves A1 to A4 and A8.

# 3. Mutation run
$ JOBS=8 node docs/validation/VTID-05540/outputs/mutate-rehearse.mjs .      -> outputs/mutation-run.txt
baseline 121 tests pass; 163 mutations, 163 caught, 0 survived, 0 not applicable. One behaviour is broken at a time in a scratch copy of scripts/eng, scripts/collab and infra/gitlab-engineering/{rehearsal,settings,ci,m2.sh}: the plan, the arguments, every refusal, the allowlists of AWS and of writes, the seed (manifest, blob id, diff, address), the three controls and the job script, the parsers, every threshold and verdict of A1, A2, A3, A4 and A8, the order of the waves, cleanup, redaction, exit codes. The first pass of this harness (161 mutations) left 14 alive; each one was traced and either the test was strengthened (opaque token fixtures so that redaction cannot hide behind token shapes, staggered boots so that the timing of the second wave shows, assertions for the AWS group name and region, the control seats of a partial run, the VTID check alone, the seed with a protected path, the missing last commit, the progress figure, the protection re-read at the end, the base commit order) or a redundant clause was removed from the code (the count check of A4 that the subject comparison already implies; a second redaction of the report). Two mutations were added for the report fallback. The harness lists its own mistakes (NOOP, AMBIGUOUS, INVALID, CRASH, HUNG count as not caught).

